KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12 --unwind 10 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ virtual base constructed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [class.base.init]/6-7: the target of istringstream's delegating
constructor constructs the virtual base basic_ios.  It used to be called
as for a base subobject and constructed none, with 42 (libstdc++) or 36
(libc++) failed properties.
With the MSVC STL the constructor is a constructor template, not a
delegating one; it failed there because the base basic_istream was
constructed as a complete object
(cpp11_base_constructor_with_default_arguments_in_class_with_virtual_base).
